"""Azshara: story speeches; accept lines are in azshara_beats."""

STORY = {
    'az_the_north_gate': ("Elder Torgun sealed this report himself, and it goes to Overseer Durgash Stonejaw at Talrendis Landing. Durgash runs Orgrimmar's half of the dig there, and the elves run the other half. The new gate out of the canyon north of the Valley of Honor opens straight onto Azshara, so it's not a long walk. The Warchief wants to know what the elves are pulling out of the ground, and he wants to know before they do. Go out the north gate and up through the forest, and you'll find the Landing on the point to the west. I've carried enough of Torgun's letters to know he seals the ones that matter, so keep it where nobody can see it until it's in Durgash's hands.", "Don't stop to talk to any elves on the road. They'll be curious about the seal."),
    'az_the_sea_side_dig': ('You unroll the map you took from the naga. It shows them digging all along the coast, with one tunnel coming in under Eldarath from the sea. The marks end at the Temple of Zin-Malor on the southern headland, drawn darker than the rest, as if somebody pressed hard there. Whoever made this knew exactly where they were going. Dr. Okafor at Talrendis Landing ought to see it before anyone takes sides.', 'You fold the map along its creases. The temple mark has worn a hole almost through the paper.'),
    'az_gatekeeper_azgaroth': ("One doomguard still stands at the gate on Forlorn Ridge, and he's the one the Legion left in charge. His name's Gatekeeper Azgaroth, and as long as he stands that gate will open again. The rite's broken, but I've felt him trying to start it again in the ground under my feet, and he could do it in an afternoon. He keeps to the gate itself and won't leave it. He hits like a falling tree and burns like one too, so bring a healer.", 'Strike the gate stones as well as him if you get the chance. Every crack you put in them buys us time.'),
    'az_the_weeping_duchess': ("One of the names on those seals is a duchess who drowned waiting for her husband to come back from the palace. She's still waiting, and the other ghosts follow her through the streets. While she walks, none of them will rest, and I've watched them try. The Weeping Duchess keeps to the heart of the Drowned Court. Her grief's a weapon, so don't let her hold you.", "Speak to her before you raise your weapon. She hasn't heard a kind voice in ten thousand years."),
    'az_haldarr_the_hornlord': ("The satyrs' lord, Haldarr, lives in the hollow at the top of the den under his encampment. Every satyr in West Azshara answers to him, and every totem they've broken was broken on his word. I've carved a replacement for every one, and it ends with him. Haldarr Den's under the encampment in the south-east of West Azshara, and you climb the taproot to his hollow. He'll pin you to the tree if you let him.", "Cut the vines on the taproot as you climb. They're his, and they'll warn him."),
}
